"Projects - The Netizen | ARCHIMATRIX Architects Malaysia (https://www.archimatrix.com.my/netizen)\nciteturn286search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Located in the residential township of Bandar Tun Hussein Onn, The Netizen is designed as two tower blocks with 536 SOHO units and 660 apartment units with broad balconies.\n\n# The Netizen\n\n##### Cheras, Selangor\n\nThe idea of ‘Total Living Concept’, or self-contained community, was the primary approach to scheme The Netizen due to market demand and its close proximity to a network of highways and an MRT Station. Located in the residential township of Bandar Tun Hussein Onn, The Netizen is designed as two tower blocks with 536 SOHO units and 660 apartment units with broad balconies. The podium below accommodates shoplots at its first two floors, with office spaces at the third floor. Generously provided amenities are a given to achieve the self- contained approach. Hence, indoor facilities were also provided such as half a basketball court and badminton court for use in either rain or shine. A Sky Deck punctures each block at level 24, breaking the building’s form while function as a platform for residents to enjoy.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProjects | ARCHIMATRIX Architects Malaysia (https://www.archimatrix.com.my/projects)\nciteturn286search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ARCHIMATRIX has never limited architecture to a particular style, type or scale of work. ... The Netizen\n\n# Projects\n\nARCHIMATRIX has never limited architecture to a particular style, type or scale of work. Our wealth of diverse building experience gives us the skills, knowledge and drive to manage many complex developments. Having observed property market cycles and kept abreast with market positions, our design philosophy and methodology focuses on the optimization of time, space and resources.\n\nWe aim to achieve complete satisfaction for all our clients and end users.\n\n### Setia Sky Seputeh\n\n##### Taman Seputeh, Kuala Lumpur\n\nThe brief is an interpretation of its locale of mostly landed bungalows, semi-detached and linked houses amongst the canopy of aging rain trees, with both community and nature continue to thrive on the hill-profile of Taman Seputeh. The project intends to contribute to this growth by offering vertical living ala-Seputeh, while celebrating the site’s topographical feature.\n\n### Skyluxe on the Park\n\n##### Bukit Jalil, Kuala Lumpur\n\nSkyLuxe on the Park celebrates its context of Bukit Jalil Recreational Park and the Golf and Country Resort. Located on a 1.85-acre site within a maturing sub-urban neighbourhood surrounded by green enclaves, the project aspired to make all 477 homes as destinations of retreat. Its emphasis on the park’s main entrance is seen as a given to establish a symbiotic connection with nature.\n\n### Plaza 33\n\n##### Petaling Jaya, Selangor\n\nStrategically located at the southern tip of Section 13 Petaling Jaya, Plaza 33 is an expansion of the existing Jaya 33 development as its second-phase offices. Previously a paint factory, the brief’s call for a new building with 500,000 ft2 of grade A offices sets a tabula rasa for the project to re-establish connectivity for the area – a busy junction, a primary school, the mature section 14 commercial enclave, an existing residential neighbourhood.\n\n### CloudTree Residence\n\n##### Seri Kembangan, Selangor\n\nThe homes of this development are built on a challenging topography, only to be advantageous to the design intent for an urban sanctuary with a resort-like ambience. Four distinct plateaus along the site’s longitudinal axis informed the placement of five apartment blocks, but significantly, a Central Park and a clubhouse were designed on the site’s valley as the heart of the development and datum point to CloudTree’s masterplan.\n\n### All projects\n\nSetia Sky Seputeh\n\nSkyluxe on the Park\n\nThe Airie\n\nCloudTree Residence\n\nNova Saujana\n\nThe Pines Hotel\n\nJaya Shopping Centre\n\nPJ21\n\nJaya 33\n\nSetia Sky Residences\n\nTrion\n\nCristal Serin Residences\n\nD’PULZE\n\nCybersquare\n\nPlaza 33\n\nCitizen 2\n\nCitizen\n\nSK One Residence\n\nBukit Bantayan Residences\n\nThe Netizen\n\nVilla 22\n\nMI Hilltop\n\nPalm Hill Residence\n\nTrion 2\n\nThe Pulse\n\nHouse at Esplanad\n\nKajang PR1MA\n\nLayered City Masterplan\n\nPanorama Residences\n\nThe Valley Residences--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProjects - Citizen | ARCHIMATRIX Architects Malaysia (https://www.archimatrix.com.my/citizen)\nciteturn286search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n# Citizen\n\n##### Old Klang Road, Kuala Lumpur\n\n##### Completed 2018\n\nCitizen is a high-rise residential development with a brief relevant to the demands of the younger market – young professionals and young families – for a well-equipped and conveniently located home. It is a distinct looking apartment as one drives along the New Pantai Expressway (NPE). At three residential towers atop a huge podium on over three acres of land, the façade comprises highly defined horizontal and vertical elements with a contrast of colours, resulting a sophisticated persona fit for the characters it contains.\n\nTwo courtyards between the three entrances on ground level are instrumental to subdue the podium with activities. Whilst the badminton courts, a forest lounge, gymnasium and yoga room at first floor have connections with these courtyards, an extensive array of facilities are designed and fitted on the podium including a futsal court, table tennis room, art studio, lounge pool, kid’s pool and a lap pool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Netizen Condo for Sale in Cheras, Selangor by GARY FONG | EdgeProp.my (https://www.edgeprop.my/listing/sale/3068370/selangor/cheras/nonlanded/condominium-apartment-servicedresidence/cheras-the-netizen-fully-furnished-unit)\nciteturn286search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: yesterday; Crawled: today; Image: Cheras the Netizen fully furnished unit , Selangor, Cheras ... The development is offering 536 Soho units and 660 Apartment units with built-up from 547sf to 1328sf, providing a vibrant space for singles, young couples and small families.\n\nImage: Cheras the Netizen fully furnished unit , Selangor, Cheras\n\nImage: Cheras the Netizen fully furnished unit , Selangor, Cheras\n\n# The Netizen\n\nThe Netizen, Taman Cheras Perdana Ria, 43200, Selangor, Cheras, Selangor\n\nRM 350,000\n\n3 Bed(s)\n\n2 Bath(s)\n\n500 sqft(built-up area)\n\nRM 700/sqft(built-up price)\n\n## Property details\n\nCondominium for sale\n\n3 Bed(s)\n\nListed on 05 Oct 2026\n\n2 Bath(s)\n\nListing ID - LIDM3068370\n\n500 sqft\n\n(built-up area)\n\nFully Furnished\n\n\n## About the listing\n\nNetizen walking distance to MRT station RESIDENSI NETIZEN Netizen bandar tun hussein onn Selling : rm350000 LBH UTAMA, BANDAR TUN HUSSEIN ONN, 43200 CHERAS SELANGOR OPEN FOR Sale ❗️❗️❗️ SOHO UNIT(500 SQFT) 🏠 FACING KL VIEW 🏙️ - 1 ROOM 🛏️ - 1 BATH 🛁 - 1 CARPARK 🚘 kindly contact Gary 0122626888 pea1619 The Netizen comprises 2 residential towers on top of a multi-level podium with 24 hours security system. The development is offering 536 Soho units and 660 Apartment units with built-up from 547sf to 1328sf, providing a vibrant space for singles, young couples and small families. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nARCHIMATRIX | Architects Malaysia (https://www.archimatrix.com.my/)\nciteturn286search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\nHome\n\n  * Studio\n  * Projects\n  * Clients\n  * Awards\n  * Contact--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Netizen @ Cheras | Lokahood (https://lokahood.com/business-page/the-netizen-cheras/)\nciteturn286search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # The Netizen @ Cheras ... This dynamic development offers 536 SOHO units and 660 Apartment units, with sizes ranging from a cosy 547 square feet to a spacious 1,328 square feet.\n## Why Netizen Cheras?\n\nNetizen Cheras is a modern mixed-use development developed by KEB Group, situated strategically at Jalan Suarasa 8/3, Bandar Tun Hussein Onn, Cheras, Selangor. Netizen Cheras combines Small Office Home Office (SOHO) and Serviced Residency, comprising two stylish towers with 38 floors each, connected via a sky bridge equipped with a 24-hour security system. \n\nThis dynamic development offers 536 SOHO units and 660 Apartment units, with sizes ranging from a cosy 547 square feet to a spacious 1,328 square feet. It caters to a diverse demographic, providing a vibrant living space ideal for singles, young couples, and small families.\n\nThe variety of units available at Netizen Cheras ranges from sleek SOHO units to comfortable 3-bedroom and 4-bedroom apartments. The design of each unit prioritises natural light, incorporating expansive windows and generous balconies. These features infuse the living spaces with various colours, creating a welcoming atmosphere.”\n\nAdding to its versatility, Netizen Cheras also boasts a commercial section encompassing two stories of shop lots on Levels 1 and 2 and a dedicated office space on Level 3. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout us | ARCHIMATRIX Architects Malaysia (https://www.archimatrix.com.my/about)\nciteturn286search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; ARCHIMATRIX is a Malaysian architectural practice with a robust portfolio of projects located throughout the country. ... ###### B Arch, Universiti Sains Malaysia (2004)\n\n# About Us\n\nARCHIMATRIX is a Malaysian architectural practice with a robust portfolio of projects located throughout the country. Based in the capital city, Kuala Lumpur, the practice majors in large- scale projects with a developer-majority clientele.\n\nARCHIMATRIX started out as a partnership in 2000 and was subsequently incorporated in 2008. Led by the two founding partners, the practice has grown from a modest-sized team to a medium-sized practice.\n\nARCHIMATRIX employs a design philosophy and methodology anchored on the optimisation of time, space and resources. Architecture will be addressed beyond any particular style, type or scale, whilst relevance with developments in the property market sector is ensured.\n\nARCHIMATRIX is equipped with the knowledge and experiences in managing many complex developments, especially in large-scale residential and commercial projects, and mixed-use developments. The practice equally provides this expertise in other project typologies.\n\n## Our Approach\n\nThe ARCHIMATRIX team is attentive, inquisitive and critical in devising a creative solution for every project brief. We are committed to create design and architectural works best for its place, beneficiaries and people. We offer creative yet functional solutions, and realising their possibilities into constructed forms to be further inhabited, explored and enjoyed by many.\n\nThe world is a never-ending arena; thus, we are determined to continuously innovate and improve, and ensuring relevance of any given project. We take our experiences and insights to the projects’ advantage, utilising our knowledge in building typologies, urban planning, effective spatial designs, building technologies, as well as project procurements and management.\n\nWe take pride in our track record of returning clienteles, as well as new clients from complimentary recommendations. We celebrate our accomplishments resulting from true collective efforts with our clients, consultants and specialists, even throughout the stages of a project. We continue seeking aspirations from future collaborations, and renewed inspirations from opportunities.\n\n### Jasper Mah\n\n##### DIRECTOR\n\n###### B Arch (Hons), University of New South Wales, Australia (1991)\n\nProfessional Associatio